<!--
Merge this into the <dict> of ios/Runner/Info.plist AND macos/Runner/Info.plist
after you run `flutter create . --platforms=ios,macos`. This registers the
"petalauth://" URL scheme so flutter_web_auth_2 can catch Microsoft's OAuth
redirect on both platforms. Must match AuthConfig.microsoftRedirectUri in
lib/data/services/auth/auth_config.dart.

apply_packaging_snippets.py ALSO adds two more keys to ios/Runner/Info.plist
ONLY (not macOS) — NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription and
NSAppleMusicUsageDescription. These aren't related to the URL scheme above;
they exist because file_picker ships one unified iOS binary that links
Photos-framework code regardless of which FileType your own code actually
calls, and Apple's App Store/TestFlight review can reject a build missing
those usage-description strings even though this app never touches Photos
or Apple Music — see IOS_USAGE_DESCRIPTIONS in apply_packaging_snippets.py
for the exact text and the GitHub issue this was verified against.
-->
<key>CFBundleURLTypes</key>
<array>
    <dict>
        <key>CFBundleURLSchemes</key>
        <array>
            <string>petalauth</string>
        </array>
        <key>CFBundleURLName</key>
        <string>com.petal.player.auth</string>
    </dict>
</array>
